@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Existing heat networks – Certify your heat networks with the Heat Network Technical Assurance Scheme (HNTAS)";
}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
        <span class="govuk-caption-l">Add a heat network</span>
        <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Existing heat networks</h1>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            When the network is entirely existing i.e. it is fully operational and supplying customers, you should not register it on this service initially. Instead, you should register it with Ofgem in order to <a href="https://www.ofgem.gov.uk/energy-regulation/low-carbon/heat-networks/comply-with-heat-networks-consumer-protection-regulations" class="govuk-link">comply with heat networks consumer protection regulations</a>
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            Ofgem will ask you about what type of heat network it is, and how much of it your organisation is responsible for, including buildings and energy centres.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            Once registered and authorised to operate via Ofgem, HNTAS will be alerted to this network and we will inform you to return to this service for technical assurance.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>